<title>SWEDEN: MoDo posts sharp fall in Q1 profit.</title>
<headline>MoDo posts sharp fall in Q1 profit.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish forestry group MoDo on Tuesday posted these earnings for the first quarter ending on March 31.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		    391 vs 858</p>
<p> Sales					 5,457 vs 5,562</p>
<p> Earnings per share (crowns)	    3.10 vs 6.60</p>
<p> Operating costs			   4,675 vs 4,288</p>
<p> Depreciation				  346 vs   286</p>
<p> Operating profit			    438 vs   990</p>
<p> Net financial items		 CHARGE 47 vs   132 CHARGE</p>
<p> Taxes					   118 vs   275</p>
<p> Net profit				    273 vs   583</p>
<p>NOTE -- Analysts expected MoDo to show a profit after financial items of 332 million crowns, a Reuter poll showed.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
